course: dictionary
lesson: 8185
title: Responsibility: a job you must look after
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A responsibility is a job or duty that someone expects you to do. «Feeding the fish is my responsibility» means nobody else has to remember it: it is your job, and you must keep doing it.
explain: Responsibility also means being trusted to do the right thing and take care, even when no one is watching. «A pet needs food, water, care, exercise and time every day: it is a responsibility, not a toy.» The sentence tells you a pet is not just fun; you must look after it every day.
explain: When something goes wrong, taking responsibility means owning up to it and putting it right. «Take responsibility for the broken window» means saying, "It was me, and I will fix it." Words like «take», «a sense of» and «it's your» are clues that the word is about duty.
fact: A responsibility is a duty or job you are expected to do or look after.
fact: Responsibility means being trusted to do the right thing and take care, without being watched.
fact: To take responsibility for a mistake means owning up to it and putting it right.
fact: Rights come with responsibilities: the freedoms you have also come with things you must do.
fact: Useful phrases: «take responsibility», «a sense of responsibility», «responsibility for», «it's your responsibility».
exercise: «Feeding the fish is my responsibility.» What is a responsibility? | *A duty or job you are expected to look after | A type of fish | A prize you win for being good | A game played at break time
exercise: «She took responsibility for the broken window and said sorry.» What does take responsibility mean here? | Blamed her little brother | Ran away before anyone saw | *Owned up to it and put it right | Asked someone else to pay for a new window
exercise: Which of these is a responsibility at school? | Winning the spelling bee | Eating your lunch | Getting a day off | *Looking after the class plants each week
test: «A pet needs food, water, care, exercise and time every day: it is a responsibility, not a toy.» What does responsibility mean here? | A type of toy | *A job you must keep doing, not just a bit of fun | A game you play with friends | A thing you only do on Sundays
test: Which word means being trusted to do the right thing when nobody is watching? | *Responsibility | Showing off | Forgetfulness | Mischief
exam: Ruby says a responsibility is a game you play at break. What is the right meaning? | *A duty or job you are expected to do or look after | A kind of holiday | A game with a ball and a whistle | Something you only do when it is raining
